# WHAT SHIPS IS client/out, server/out, THEIR node_modules, AND THE STATIC
# CONTRIBUTIONS (syntaxes, snippets, language-configuration.json, images).
# Everything else is excluded here.
#
# `vsce package` WALKS THE WORKING TREE, NOT GIT. Nothing in .gitignore is
# excluded by virtue of being ignored, and that is the whole reason this file
# needed rewriting: ivpm populates packages/ with ~500 MB that git never sees
# and vsce packaged all of it.
#
# A DIRECTORY SYMLINK IN THE FILE LIST IS A HARD FAILURE, not a size problem.
# vsce lists a symlinked directory as ONE entry and secretlint then read()s it
# as a file, which is EISDIR -- `Error occurred while scanning secrets (files)`
# and exit 1, with no indication of which path did it. The ivpm tree carries
# seven such symlinks (packages/python/lib64, the three skills/ivpm links,
# packages/pssparser/packages/emsdk, and the two @psstools/pssparser links).
# Every pattern below that covers one of those is load-bearing for the build
# passing at all -- not a size optimisation.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# ivpm's working tree. Not source, not runtime: fetched dependencies and
# their build trees. packages/pssparser alone is 305 MB of C++ and Emscripten
# output, packages/python is a 190 MB venv.
#
# NOTE ON THE PARSER. While server/package.json names the parser as
# `file:../packages/pssparser/ts`, npm links it as a SYMLINK into packages/,
# so excluding packages/ leaves that link dangling. It cannot be fixed by
# re-including packages/pssparser/ts/dist: vsce would still emit the link
# itself as a single entry, which is the EISDIR above. The fix is the
# published @psstools/pssparser -- npm then writes a real directory into
# server/node_modules and it ships through the server/node_modules rule with
# no special case here. See the note next to that rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
packages/**
ivpm.yaml
packages.envrc

# Agent skill directories, populated by ivpm as symlinks into packages/python.
.agents/**
.claude/**
.cursor/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Repository and CI machinery.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
.git/**
.gitignore
.gitmodules
.github/**
.forgejo/**
azure-pipelines.yml
.eslintrc.json
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
ws.vscode-pss-support-lsp.code-workspace
vsc-extension-quickstart.md
*.vsix

# ROOT node_modules ONLY -- client/node_modules and server/node_modules are
# the runtime trees and are NOT matched by this pattern. The root manifest
# declares no `dependencies`, only devDependencies (typescript, eslint,
# vitest, vsce), so nothing here is needed at runtime. vsce already drops it
# via `npm list --prod` returning empty, but that is a resolution result
# rather than a stated intent; if a root runtime dependency is ever added,
# this line is what has to change.
node_modules/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Sources, tests and docs. The compiled out/ trees are what run.
#
# `**/*.ts` also covers vitest.config.ts and every .d.ts under node_modules;
# nothing resolves a .d.ts at runtime.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------- #
**/*.ts
**/tsconfig*.json
**/*.map
docs/**
test/**
server/test/**
server/bench/**
client/test/**
*.g4

# Grammar sources for the TextMate build live here; the built JSON in
# syntaxes/ is what VS Code loads.
**/.env

# Stray build-log file of the same name as the (excluded) out/ directories.
# `out` matches only the root path, so client/out and server/out are untouched.
out
